                "entry_id": "0cd26d6c-5a59-38d9-839b-190498d749be",
                "word": "inclémence",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3be8fa52-9657-4db5-97f5-4bcda78ee726",
                        "entry_id": "0cd26d6c-5a59-38d9-839b-190498d749be",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "inclémences"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "10e9dae9-7f84-3985-90eb-c404d6cb6721",
                        "entry_id": "0cd26d6c-5a59-38d9-839b-190498d749be",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Défaut de clémence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "40252da3-06e9-43c1-8fc8-8c26b414ccd2",
                                "sense_id": "10e9dae9-7f84-3985-90eb-c404d6cb6721",
                                "text": "Ce devait être assez, dit Denys d'Halicarnasse, pour que de telles marques d'humanité rendissent les esclaves dociles, attachés à leurs maîtres, et disposés à supporter, pendant tout le reste de l'année, l’inclémence de la fortune à leur égard."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "901cffb6-e065-45fe-8eb4-f6f7084fef8a",
                                "sense_id": "10e9dae9-7f84-3985-90eb-c404d6cb6721",
                                "text": "Il virera selon les saisons de la nature et l’inclémence des hommes au pourpre ou au safran, mais cette coloration pistache le long de l’Yser relevait, elle, d’une intention maléfique."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8641c5fc-846d-3ad2-8aa7-51372c901ff1",
                        "entry_id": "0cd26d6c-5a59-38d9-839b-190498d749be",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Rigueur excessive."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1eb5ac4c-5fcd-4a1b-bd90-f9ae73ac452c",
                                "sense_id": "8641c5fc-846d-3ad2-8aa7-51372c901ff1",
                                "text": "L’inclémence de la critique."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a0a57954-88a9-4371-ab39-a6b502c0a7f3",
                                "sense_id": "8641c5fc-846d-3ad2-8aa7-51372c901ff1",
                                "text": "Des navires … courent obliquement, puis reviennent ; on dirait qu’ils se trouvent bien dans ce grand port d’eau douce ; ils s’y attardent et jouissent de sa paix au sortir des colères et de l’inclémence de l’Océan."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1f02fdf2-2988-369c-952d-e5851416a291",
                        "entry_id": "0cd26d6c-5a59-38d9-839b-190498d749be",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Âpreté, dureté, au sujet des saisons."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e7c4a92-0940-4cee-a4c8-8fd343885759",
                                "sense_id": "1f02fdf2-2988-369c-952d-e5851416a291",
                                "text": "Pendant ces deux jours, l’averse ne cessa pas, mais qu’importe ? cette inclémence météorologique n’altéra en rien la grande et profonde impression de l’Océan vu."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d370035d-9f52-4d4a-b5a6-be4ad144a5ba",
                                "sense_id": "1f02fdf2-2988-369c-952d-e5851416a291",
                                "text": "L’habitation n'est pas la seule protection qu’ait cherchée l’Homme. Son corps aussi a besoin d’être protégé, aussi bien de l’inclémence du temps que des autres dangers qui l’environnent."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4d64c80d-aeaf-42f1-8ecb-ed81bcdbcfa1",
                        "source_entry_id": "0cd26d6c-5a59-38d9-839b-190498d749be",
                        "target_lang_word": "inclemency",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "inclemency",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b4efe700-7925-3b36-b46f-efa7f0506766",
                                        "entry_id": "1fd5d318-de7e-3cb6-b070-918e79ea6543",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of being inclement; lack of clemency."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "34662a9f-5599-3848-a391-ec04e148813f",
                                        "entry_id": "1fd5d318-de7e-3cb6-b070-918e79ea6543",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something that is inclement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "943d3dab-fed1-4b4d-8ce3-c138324f5dfc",
                                                "sense_id": "34662a9f-5599-3848-a391-ec04e148813f",
                                                "text": "with neither house nor clothes to cover them from the inclemencies of the weather"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf7a6c66-8b72-4cc8-8194-aa7df78ea09d",
                                                "sense_id": "34662a9f-5599-3848-a391-ec04e148813f",
                                                "text": "They are built of rough sticks, covered with bulrushes or grass, in such a manner as to completely protect the inhabitants from all the inclemencies of the weather."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4967852c-a1ba-487d-ac50-a7bf0115cf8e",
                                                "sense_id": "34662a9f-5599-3848-a391-ec04e148813f",
                                                "text": "There had been rain, squalls mingled with snow, hailstorms, gusts of wind, but these inclemencies did not last."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae5008e8-cc38-4bf7-b7f0-371726cd3a8e",
                                                "sense_id": "34662a9f-5599-3848-a391-ec04e148813f",
                                                "text": "The cry of the suffering and dying rings in our ears, as they are dragged from their beds, to be exposed to the inclemencies of the ice-covered sea in an open boat."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
